# Application-specific skills never ship in the image.
#
# `COPY sage_skills /tmp/build/skills` copies the DIRECTORY, not the tracked
# files, so anything sitting in sage_skills/ on the build host is baked in --
# including skills git never sees. A skill for one application is delivered
# with %%skill instead, from a public repo or a local path, which also keeps a
# baked copy from silently shadowing the one a notebook declares.
#
# Add a line here when a new application skill lands in sage_skills/.
sage_skills/amaro-datasets/
